<p id="mwAlk">Max Planck Society also has a collaborative center with <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Princeton_University" title="Princeton University" id="mwAlo">Princeton University</a>—<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Max_Planck_Princeton_Research_Center_for_Plasma_Physics?action=edit&amp;redlink=1" title="Max Planck Princeton Research Center for Plasma Physics" class="new" typeof="mw:LocalizedAttrs" data-mw-i18n='{"title":{"lang":"x-page","key":"red-link-title","params":["Max Planck Princeton Research Center for Plasma Physics"]}}' id="mwAls">Max Planck Princeton Research Center for Plasma Physics</a>—located in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Princeton,_New_Jersey" title="Princeton, New Jersey" id="mwAlw">Princeton, New Jersey</a>, in the U.S.<sup about="#mwt89" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-MPGPrinceton_21-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"MPGPrinceton"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-MPGPrinceton-21"}}'><a href="./Max_Planck_Society#cite_note-MPGPrinceton-21" id="mwAl0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAl4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAl8">[</span>21<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAmA">]</span></span></a></sup> The latest Max Planck Research Center has been established at <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Harvard_University" title="Harvard University" id="mwAmE">Harvard University</a> in 2016 as the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Max_Planck_Harvard_Research_Center_for_the_Archaeoscience_of_the_Ancient_Mediterranean" title="Max Planck Harvard Research Center for the Archaeoscience of the Ancient Mediterranean" id="mwAmI">Max Planck Harvard Research Center for the Archaeoscience of the Ancient Mediterranean</a>.</p>

